1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,280
No!

2
00:00:04,840 --> 00:00:05,480
Valon!

3
00:00:06,480 --> 00:00:09,380
Can she even be revived after all that?

4
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:13,380
I've heard that it's been done before, but...

5
00:00:13,380 --> 00:00:16,560
Hey, Laios? What are you...

6
00:00:16,560 --> 00:00:19,280
The Resurrection Office. They'll know what to do.

7
00:00:20,060 --> 00:00:21,880
Are you planning to take everything?

8
00:00:22,440 --> 00:00:24,320
But aren't Wargbones mixed in there, too?

9
00:00:24,840 --> 00:00:26,280
It's hard to tell them apart.

10
00:00:28,080 --> 00:00:28,980
Let me help.

11
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,600
Please wait!

12
00:00:33,860 --> 00:00:37,000
The link between the soul and body is fragile now.

13
00:00:37,280 --> 00:00:38,440
You shouldn't move her.

14
00:00:39,220 --> 00:00:42,700
The more damaged the body is, the weaker the soul's bond.

15
00:00:43,180 --> 00:00:47,380
When a Resurrection fails, it's usually because the soul separated too far,

16
00:00:47,660 --> 00:00:49,820
or because the body wasn't fully restored.

17
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:51,600
Then what should we do?

18
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:55,820
We go get a Revival Specialist and revive her here.

19
00:00:55,820 --> 00:01:01,100
But the Restoration requires more than twice the amount of calories for the damaged parts,

20
00:01:01,320 --> 00:01:04,700
so we'd also need to bring a lot of fresh meat for it to work.

21
00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:07,200
It would rot on the way down, wouldn't it?

22
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:07,860
Hang on.

23
00:01:07,860 --> 00:01:08,060
Huh?

24
00:01:08,860 --> 00:01:09,360
Yes.

25
00:01:09,920 --> 00:01:13,820
We have a large amount of fresh meat right here in front of us.

26
00:01:13,820 --> 00:01:16,340
Hey, now hold on a sec.

27
00:01:16,640 --> 00:01:19,220
You're gonna resurrect her with Dragon Meat?

28
00:01:19,920 --> 00:01:21,720
Reviving isn't even your specialty.

29
00:01:21,720 --> 00:01:26,340
I didn't want to scare anyone, so I never mentioned it.

30
00:01:26,340 --> 00:01:32,200
What I specialize in is actually ancient magic, which is highly forbidden.

31
00:01:33,140 --> 00:01:38,220
Its use is frowned upon, but using it to revive Falon, it's our best option.

32
00:01:38,360 --> 00:01:38,860
Marcil!

33
00:01:38,860 --> 00:01:40,100
Black magic?

34
00:01:40,460 --> 00:01:41,540
That stuff is evil.

35
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:44,320
Magic doesn't have morality.

36
00:01:46,760 --> 00:01:49,500
Well, Lyos, it's your choice.

37
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:51,520
Please do it, Marcil.

38
00:01:52,080 --> 00:01:54,160
Bring my sister back from the dead.

39
00:01:56,540 --> 00:01:57,540
All right, then.

40
00:01:57,880 --> 00:01:58,420
I'll try.

41
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:00,340
Are you guys insane?

42
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:02,560
Using Dragon Meat, of all things.

43
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:05,640
Goat and pig are what people would normally use for this,

44
00:02:05,740 --> 00:02:07,180
but we don't have that right now.

45
00:02:07,380 --> 00:02:08,720
All right, let's start.

46
00:02:08,860 --> 00:02:26,500
First things first, I would like to put the body back in its original shape,

47
00:02:26,620 --> 00:02:28,640
so I'll start assembling her skeleton.

48
00:02:29,060 --> 00:02:30,100
That makes sense.

49
00:02:30,580 --> 00:02:32,340
I'm familiar with canine skeletons,

50
00:02:32,340 --> 00:02:35,140
so I'll work on putting the wargs together.

51
00:02:35,140 --> 00:02:40,460
That's kind of unnecessary, isn't it?

52
00:02:40,500 --> 00:02:43,520
Not if it helps us avoid missing something or making dumb mistakes!

53
00:02:45,740 --> 00:02:47,900
Humans have around 200 bones.

54
00:02:48,360 --> 00:02:51,480
Then we're looking at about 840 bones total.

55
00:02:51,900 --> 00:02:52,240
Huh?

56
00:02:52,440 --> 00:02:53,500
How do you know that?

57
00:02:54,460 --> 00:02:56,540
Dogs have around 320 bones,

58
00:02:56,660 --> 00:02:58,060
and there are two skulls here,

59
00:02:58,200 --> 00:02:59,220
so it's easy math.

60
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:02,220
Let's start with the most recognizable ones.

61
00:03:02,920 --> 00:03:05,100
The rounder set is a human's ribcage,

62
00:03:05,300 --> 00:03:08,260
and the spine is directly connected to the ribs.

63
00:03:08,440 --> 00:03:09,740
Their curves don't look the same,

64
00:03:09,860 --> 00:03:11,080
so they're easy to tell apart.

65
00:03:11,640 --> 00:03:15,120
The toughest ones are the smaller bones from the hands and feet.

66
00:03:15,580 --> 00:03:18,140
Yeah, it's a lot harder to tell the difference.

67
00:03:18,140 --> 00:03:21,280
Let's start with the bigger pieces and work down.

68
00:03:22,020 --> 00:03:24,420
This piece that I'm holding is the ankle bone.

69
00:03:25,040 --> 00:03:26,440
Find the next biggest one,

70
00:03:26,640 --> 00:03:28,780
then connect the two sides that line up,

71
00:03:28,980 --> 00:03:30,620
and the instep is complete.

72
00:03:31,960 --> 00:03:34,360
And then we have the bones from the hands.

73
00:03:34,740 --> 00:03:36,760
Let's arrange them starting with the fingers.

74
00:03:37,020 --> 00:03:37,720
I got it!

75
00:03:39,240 --> 00:03:40,420
Like this, right?

76
00:03:41,340 --> 00:03:42,340
So close.

77
00:03:42,900 --> 00:03:44,720
Actually, the longest metacarpal,

78
00:03:44,880 --> 00:03:46,040
despite what you might think,

79
00:03:46,040 --> 00:03:47,500
goes on the pointer finger.

80
00:03:48,140 --> 00:03:49,620
That just leaves us with the ones

81
00:03:49,620 --> 00:03:51,320
that connect the fingers to the wrist.

82
00:03:57,040 --> 00:03:57,980
Hint, please!

83
00:03:58,100 --> 00:03:59,660
This isn't a game, Lyos!

84
00:04:03,240 --> 00:04:03,760
There.

85
00:04:04,820 --> 00:04:05,600
It's ready!

86
00:04:09,340 --> 00:04:10,720
How do I put this?

87
00:04:11,600 --> 00:04:13,280
What a beautiful skeleton.

88
00:04:13,720 --> 00:04:15,300
Not bad for some bones.

89
00:04:15,300 --> 00:04:17,260
Seems she had good calcium intake.

90
00:04:18,140 --> 00:04:20,860
This isn't going to revive the wargs, too, is it?

91
00:04:21,320 --> 00:04:23,600
Only human souls get bound to the dungeon.

92
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:24,920
Because otherwise,

93
00:04:25,440 --> 00:04:27,800
this place would burst from all the monster souls.

94
00:04:27,800 --> 00:04:39,420
All right.

95
00:04:39,420 --> 00:04:40,640
Here we go.

96
00:04:40,640 --> 00:04:40,660
Here we go.

97
00:04:40,660 --> 00:04:43,660
And you guys are moving.

98
00:04:48,440 --> 00:04:49,500
We will keep living.

99
00:04:49,920 --> 00:04:50,620
Here we go.

100
00:04:50,620 --> 00:04:51,040
Thank you.

101
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:51,580
I don't care.

102
00:04:51,580 --> 00:04:52,020
Let's see.

103
00:04:52,020 --> 00:04:52,640
I don't think.

104
00:04:52,640 --> 00:04:52,700
I don't think.

105
00:04:53,360 --> 00:04:53,940
I don't think.

106
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:54,060
I don't think.

107
00:04:56,160 --> 00:04:56,880
I don't think.

108
00:04:58,960 --> 00:04:59,740
Oh set.

109
00:04:59,740 --> 00:05:00,240
Marcelle!

110
00:05:15,320 --> 00:05:16,280
Marcelle!

111
00:05:18,880 --> 00:05:20,300
She just fainted.

112
00:05:21,200 --> 00:05:22,400
So what happened?

113
00:05:22,780 --> 00:05:23,880
Did it actually work?

114
00:05:29,740 --> 00:05:43,340
Fallon!

115
00:05:44,560 --> 00:05:46,360
Her airway's full of blood!

116
00:05:47,100 --> 00:05:48,720
All right, just cough it out.

117
00:05:49,860 --> 00:05:51,480
There, all good.

118
00:05:56,480 --> 00:05:57,040
Fallon.

119
00:05:59,740 --> 00:06:13,840
I'm glad you're safe.

120
00:06:16,600 --> 00:06:17,600
You're cold.

121
00:06:18,820 --> 00:06:20,420
Right! My armor, sorry.

122
00:06:20,740 --> 00:06:21,980
Let me go get you some clothes.

123
00:06:24,980 --> 00:06:26,380
Fallon, what's the matter?

124
00:06:27,680 --> 00:06:29,260
You're feeling okay, right?

125
00:06:30,700 --> 00:06:32,380
Good. I'm glad to hear it.

126
00:06:33,300 --> 00:06:33,580
Marcel.

127
00:06:34,640 --> 00:06:35,200
Marcel!

128
00:06:38,020 --> 00:06:39,120
How's Fallon?

129
00:06:39,780 --> 00:06:40,880
Alive and well.

130
00:06:41,700 --> 00:06:43,380
But she's still a bit disoriented.

131
00:06:49,740 --> 00:06:50,540
Fallon!

132
00:06:50,540 --> 00:06:50,820
Fallon!

133
00:06:50,820 --> 00:06:57,900
I'm so glad. Thank goodness.

134
00:06:59,460 --> 00:06:59,920
Marcel.

135
00:06:59,920 --> 00:07:00,100
Marcel.

136
00:07:08,100 --> 00:07:09,000
Chill, Chuck.

137
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:10,520
How are you feeling?

138
00:07:11,800 --> 00:07:14,100
She's still kind of confused about this.

139
00:07:14,720 --> 00:07:19,900
All right. This guy here? His name's Senshi. He's been a big help during our journey.

140
00:07:20,900 --> 00:07:24,180
Good to meet you, Fallon. I've heard a lot about you.

141
00:07:25,560 --> 00:07:26,140
Senshi.

142
00:07:26,140 --> 00:07:36,700
Seems like a good time to start prepping a meal.

143
00:07:40,700 --> 00:07:46,840
Thank goodness. I was so worried, Fallon. I'm so happy. I bet everything worked out in the end.

144
00:07:46,840 --> 00:07:48,240
Uh, Marcel?

145
00:07:48,240 --> 00:07:48,800
Hmm?

146
00:07:48,800 --> 00:07:50,700
I can wash myself, you know?

147
00:07:51,180 --> 00:07:54,460
Yeah, but I wanted to make sure your skin was properly restored.

148
00:07:54,800 --> 00:07:55,860
That tickles!

149
00:07:57,300 --> 00:07:57,820
Yes.

150
00:07:58,520 --> 00:07:59,000
Good.

151
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:02,400
Why is there a news here?

152
00:08:03,240 --> 00:08:07,580
That's the mark I got from tripping and hitting the edge of the stairs when I was a little kid.

153
00:08:07,700 --> 00:08:08,860
Oh, that's all?

154
00:08:10,200 --> 00:08:10,680
Marcel.

155
00:08:11,580 --> 00:08:13,560
You look even paler than I do.

156
00:08:14,060 --> 00:08:16,120
That's because I don't have any mana.

157
00:08:16,760 --> 00:08:19,460
If I eat something and get rest, I should be fi-

158
00:08:19,460 --> 00:08:21,260
Huh?

159
00:08:24,420 --> 00:08:25,960
What are you-

160
00:08:25,960 --> 00:08:29,400
Sorry if I scared you. I was trying to give you some of my mana.

161
00:08:29,780 --> 00:08:34,420
You don't have to do that. I don't even think you have enough to share with me right now, do you?

162
00:08:34,860 --> 00:08:40,060
I actually feel good. Like there's power welling deep inside of me.

163
00:08:41,240 --> 00:08:47,300
Fallon, you're still on the mend. So please, don't use magic until you're used to your body again.

164
00:08:50,040 --> 00:08:51,860
I died, didn't I?

165
00:08:51,860 --> 00:08:56,320
I... I don't really remember much about it.

166
00:08:57,520 --> 00:08:58,660
What happened exactly?

167
00:08:59,540 --> 00:09:01,820
You were all covered in wounds and...

168
00:09:01,820 --> 00:09:03,860
For the red dragon to appear here...

169
00:09:04,420 --> 00:09:06,200
Wait, are Shiro and Namaari okay?

170
00:09:06,780 --> 00:09:10,620
I would feel just awful if anyone risked their lives and got hurt because of me.

171
00:09:10,860 --> 00:09:12,100
No, they're all fine.

172
00:09:12,180 --> 00:09:15,860
Also, that magic circle I saw...

173
00:09:16,580 --> 00:09:19,440
There was something that just didn't feel right about it.

174
00:09:19,440 --> 00:09:25,880
I'm so sorry. It's all my fault you had to use something like that.

175
00:09:28,140 --> 00:09:29,120
Stop worrying!

176
00:09:30,860 --> 00:09:34,220
Sure, we ran into some hardships. Things got pretty rough.

177
00:09:34,640 --> 00:09:37,320
But it's easy to look back and laugh at all that now.

178
00:09:37,540 --> 00:09:39,580
Because everything turned out well in the end.

179
00:09:40,580 --> 00:09:43,620
Fallon, there's no need for you to blame yourself.

180
00:09:44,280 --> 00:09:46,720
No one regrets anything that we've been through.

181
00:09:46,720 --> 00:09:57,180
As for that magic circle, things will be fine if we erase it.

182
00:09:58,640 --> 00:10:00,100
For the moment...

183
00:10:00,100 --> 00:10:03,860
Our biggest concern is how to safely get back home.

184
00:10:04,380 --> 00:10:06,740
Oh! I still have to wash all my clothes.

185
00:10:06,920 --> 00:10:08,900
And we still have to find you a new outfit.

186
00:10:09,420 --> 00:10:11,680
Ugh, if it weren't for those stupid frogs.

187
00:10:12,240 --> 00:10:13,040
There were frogs?

188
00:10:13,040 --> 00:10:16,180
What do we do now?

189
00:10:17,320 --> 00:10:18,400
Return to the surface.

190
00:10:19,400 --> 00:10:22,060
We can't use return magic or the orcs' tunnels.

191
00:10:22,360 --> 00:10:24,660
So we'll have to get to the castle from the main road.

192
00:10:25,080 --> 00:10:25,920
Not what I meant.

193
00:10:26,660 --> 00:10:30,560
You may have rescued your sister, but the fact remains that we're still broke.

194
00:10:31,020 --> 00:10:33,200
I do have some savings in the bank, you know.

195
00:10:33,700 --> 00:10:35,240
But no promissory note.

196
00:10:35,760 --> 00:10:37,760
And it'll take a month to reproduce it.

197
00:10:37,760 --> 00:10:39,620
Yeah, you're right.

198
00:10:41,900 --> 00:10:45,100
So about that Marcel, the black magic she used.

199
00:10:45,240 --> 00:10:46,980
Did you already know she had that ability?

200
00:10:47,540 --> 00:10:49,520
I never asked her about the details.

201
00:10:49,940 --> 00:10:52,900
But she had mentioned wanting to go into a dungeon to study it.

202
00:10:53,260 --> 00:10:54,820
It always seemed weird to me.

203
00:10:55,400 --> 00:10:58,960
An elf who looked like she was living pretty comfy wanting to go into a dungeon.

204
00:10:59,500 --> 00:11:01,920
You don't suppose she's one of those dark elves, do you?

205
00:11:01,920 --> 00:11:05,700
I don't want her causing any problems for us.

206
00:11:06,200 --> 00:11:08,420
Who are you calling a dark elf?

207
00:11:10,060 --> 00:11:12,980
If dark magic was harmless, it wouldn't be forbidden.

208
00:11:13,540 --> 00:11:14,120
Oh yeah?

209
00:11:14,500 --> 00:11:16,480
So you'd consider healing magic harmless?

210
00:11:17,400 --> 00:11:19,220
Because even that can be used for torture.

211
00:11:19,220 --> 00:11:23,300
I'm researching ways that forbidden magic can be useful to people.

212
00:11:23,960 --> 00:11:25,900
And honestly, I'm not ashamed of it.

213
00:11:27,460 --> 00:11:32,480
Although I think it's for the best if we forget about the method of resurrection this time around, if that's okay.

214
00:11:32,720 --> 00:11:34,840
Didn't you just say that you weren't ashamed of it?

215
00:11:36,300 --> 00:11:37,220
It's fine.

216
00:11:37,440 --> 00:11:38,820
It's all over anyway.

217
00:11:39,660 --> 00:11:41,060
I just realized.

218
00:11:41,060 --> 00:11:48,680
Where'd Senshi go?

219
00:11:49,220 --> 00:11:50,660
Maybe dealing with the dragon meat?

220
00:11:51,180 --> 00:11:53,080
Oh, I just passed Mr. Senshi.

221
00:11:53,300 --> 00:11:55,520
He was carrying a giant pan along with firewood.

222
00:11:55,840 --> 00:11:58,080
Like I said, he's prepping food.

223
00:11:59,520 --> 00:12:00,040
Food?

224
00:12:00,980 --> 00:12:02,220
Near the dragon?

225
00:12:04,920 --> 00:12:06,300
We've got to stop him!

226
00:12:06,580 --> 00:12:07,320
What's happening?

227
00:12:07,600 --> 00:12:10,080
When I cut open the dragon, I cut the fuel organ.

228
00:12:10,080 --> 00:12:14,080
So lighting a fire close to it is gonna...

229
00:12:14,080 --> 00:12:14,860
Senshi!

230
00:12:15,500 --> 00:12:17,120
Please, stop!

231
00:12:35,040 --> 00:12:37,120
He... he's alive.

232
00:12:37,440 --> 00:12:39,380
Is this defensive magic?

233
00:12:40,080 --> 00:12:46,040
Falon, did you cast that?

234
00:12:46,700 --> 00:12:47,740
I think so.

235
00:12:47,780 --> 00:12:50,320
How'd you do it so fast and without chanting?

236
00:12:51,160 --> 00:12:52,260
I don't know.

237
00:12:52,860 --> 00:12:54,860
I thought about needing to protect everyone.

238
00:12:55,240 --> 00:12:56,320
And then...

239
00:12:56,320 --> 00:12:58,020
That's amazing.

240
00:12:58,560 --> 00:13:00,460
Is this that sudden heroic strength thing?

241
00:13:01,080 --> 00:13:04,240
Sure would have been real helpful to have when we were fighting the red dragon.

242
00:13:04,240 --> 00:13:10,360
Anyway, you were revived not that long ago, so please, refrain from using any more magic.

243
00:13:11,320 --> 00:13:12,620
That startled me.

244
00:13:13,040 --> 00:13:16,260
Didn't I say that dragons breathe fire from fuel they produce?

245
00:13:16,760 --> 00:13:18,080
You ignited that fuel.

246
00:13:18,940 --> 00:13:20,320
It's not going out, huh?

247
00:13:20,320 --> 00:13:22,320
The fat inside the body is burning.

248
00:13:22,320 --> 00:13:24,320
It'll die down eventually.

249
00:13:24,320 --> 00:13:27,980
If that's the case, then I can't take the meat from in there.

250
00:13:27,980 --> 00:13:30,100
Hmm, not good.

251
00:13:30,100 --> 00:13:35,440
I guess I'll use that fire to cook.

252
00:13:35,440 --> 00:13:40,200
Mix flour, yeast, salt, and water in a bowl and knead well.

253
00:13:40,820 --> 00:13:42,100
Let it rest for a bit.

254
00:13:42,480 --> 00:13:44,160
Go take a bath while it rests.

255
00:13:45,100 --> 00:13:47,200
Shape it to your lichen as you stretch it out.

256
00:13:47,680 --> 00:13:49,340
And add your choice of toppings.

257
00:13:50,160 --> 00:13:52,840
Lightly sprinkle flour onto a piece of dragon hide.

258
00:13:52,840 --> 00:13:55,480
Then place it inside the dragon.

259
00:13:56,720 --> 00:13:58,820
Cut off the tip of the dragon's tail.

260
00:13:59,080 --> 00:14:00,780
Ah, that's so wasteful!

261
00:14:01,080 --> 00:14:03,260
Now skin it and place it in a soup.

262
00:14:03,840 --> 00:14:05,740
Cut the meat into a block shape.

263
00:14:06,380 --> 00:14:11,420
Place it on a heated scale, and after both sides are seared, dip it into some seasoning.

264
00:14:16,280 --> 00:14:17,180
It's ready.

265
00:14:21,680 --> 00:14:22,620
Oh, man.

266
00:14:22,840 --> 00:14:23,840
Looks delicious.

267
00:14:25,600 --> 00:14:26,880
Is this okay to eat?

268
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:28,240
Of course it isn't!

269
00:14:38,420 --> 00:14:38,820
Tasty!

270
00:14:39,540 --> 00:14:41,960
Feels like the first good meal I've eaten in a while.

271
00:14:42,200 --> 00:14:42,980
Good, good.

272
00:14:43,120 --> 00:14:44,700
Take your revenge on that dragon.

273
00:14:45,080 --> 00:14:46,600
I guess it's fine.

274
00:14:46,900 --> 00:14:48,580
I'm just glad that she's feeling better.

275
00:14:52,840 --> 00:14:58,580
It's pretty tough.

276
00:14:58,820 --> 00:15:00,500
The flavor seems kind of familiar.

277
00:15:00,840 --> 00:15:02,660
Yeah, I can't really place it.

278
00:15:03,060 --> 00:15:04,980
I don't think it's cow or pig, though.

279
00:15:05,500 --> 00:15:08,100
If anything, it kind of tastes like...

280
00:15:08,100 --> 00:15:10,740
It's a bit like living armor, isn't it?

281
00:15:10,780 --> 00:15:11,860
Huh, you think so?

282
00:15:11,860 --> 00:15:14,740
I don't taste the same rusty tinge the armor had.

283
00:15:15,320 --> 00:15:19,420
The Kelpie and Frog were pretty soft, so maybe it's more like the basilisk?

284
00:15:20,020 --> 00:15:21,460
What do you think, Lyos?

285
00:15:21,460 --> 00:15:26,760
What are you all even talking about?

286
00:15:26,860 --> 00:15:28,060
This color!

287
00:15:28,600 --> 00:15:29,800
This firm texture!

288
00:15:30,540 --> 00:15:31,620
The rich flavor!

289
00:15:32,120 --> 00:15:34,140
Each of these things are distinctly unique!

290
00:15:34,140 --> 00:15:37,980
So why are you comparing the taste of this to anything else?

291
00:15:38,780 --> 00:15:41,520
Because this is the flavor of a dragon!

292
00:15:46,800 --> 00:15:51,400
Uh, uh, Fallon, you may have realized by now, but...

293
00:15:51,400 --> 00:15:55,060
We haven't had the resources to buy food, so we've been eating monsters...

294
00:15:55,060 --> 00:15:58,100
So cool!

295
00:15:58,720 --> 00:16:00,580
That is so cool!

296
00:16:00,580 --> 00:16:04,360
What kind of monsters did you eat, and how did you eat them? Tell me!

297
00:16:04,980 --> 00:16:06,040
Worried for nothing.

298
00:16:06,620 --> 00:16:08,280
This is the worst possible outcome!

299
00:16:08,760 --> 00:16:10,420
We ate a scorpion and a slime.

300
00:16:11,220 --> 00:16:12,820
Even a walking mushroom.

301
00:16:13,120 --> 00:16:14,160
No way! You did?

302
00:16:14,700 --> 00:16:17,380
We harvested vegetables from some golems, too.

303
00:16:17,800 --> 00:16:19,880
Wow! You ate a fish, man?

304
00:16:20,400 --> 00:16:22,600
That wasn't... an option.

305
00:16:23,020 --> 00:16:24,760
We did eat some living armor, though.

306
00:16:24,800 --> 00:16:26,420
Huh? How'd you do that?

307
00:16:26,980 --> 00:16:27,780
Let's see.

308
00:16:28,120 --> 00:16:30,540
The armor is basically the outer shell.

309
00:16:30,580 --> 00:16:33,620
And then, inside is a mollusk colony, which...

310
00:16:33,620 --> 00:16:36,200
Wouldn't it be a lot faster to show her the real thing?

311
00:16:39,280 --> 00:16:39,680
Huh?

312
00:16:39,900 --> 00:16:41,040
What's this about?

313
00:16:41,140 --> 00:16:41,300
Shh!

314
00:16:44,120 --> 00:16:44,480
Huh?

315
00:16:47,720 --> 00:16:48,200
Laius!

316
00:16:48,340 --> 00:16:49,740
Why'd you keep this from us?

317
00:16:49,860 --> 00:16:50,860
I'm so sorry.

318
00:16:51,340 --> 00:16:53,040
Oh, adorable.

319
00:16:53,500 --> 00:16:54,320
Can I touch?

320
00:16:54,320 --> 00:16:59,580
Oh, it went back in.

321
00:16:59,580 --> 00:17:04,920
It moves around on its own.

322
00:17:05,200 --> 00:17:05,640
Seriously?

323
00:17:06,840 --> 00:17:07,320
Sorry.

324
00:17:08,140 --> 00:17:11,400
It was only supposed to tide me over until I found another weapon.

325
00:17:11,840 --> 00:17:14,460
But it reacts to other monsters, which is convenient.

326
00:17:15,120 --> 00:17:17,340
You were oddly perceptive at times.

327
00:17:17,460 --> 00:17:19,540
Should have had Nomari appraise it for us.

328
00:17:19,640 --> 00:17:23,560
In that situation, I probably would have also thought to hold onto it.

329
00:17:23,560 --> 00:17:29,040
But tell everyone next time, if you lose the trust of those around you, you lose everything.

330
00:17:29,840 --> 00:17:31,120
I won't do it again.

331
00:17:31,480 --> 00:17:32,480
You have my word.

332
00:17:32,780 --> 00:17:33,240
All right.

333
00:17:33,420 --> 00:17:34,580
So what's your plan now?

334
00:17:34,580 --> 00:17:37,160
I'd like to keep it until I get another weapon.

335
00:17:37,700 --> 00:17:40,040
I can kill it if I submerge it in water.

336
00:17:40,040 --> 00:17:44,160
But I'd have to break the sword to get it out, or it would just rot in there.

337
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:45,320
That's not good.

338
00:17:45,560 --> 00:17:46,960
Guess we'll keep an eye on it.

339
00:17:47,580 --> 00:17:50,360
Aren't you the one who said monsters are dangerous creatures?

340
00:17:51,500 --> 00:17:53,860
And trust me, I haven't forgotten about that.

341
00:17:54,220 --> 00:17:58,520
I figured after I'd made it harmless, I could just go on and use it however I felt like.

342
00:17:58,520 --> 00:18:00,360
Well, I guess I was wrong.

343
00:18:00,960 --> 00:18:03,500
It's too difficult to use monsters while they're still alive.

344
00:18:04,560 --> 00:18:06,080
What does it taste like, brother?

345
00:18:06,680 --> 00:18:07,840
Do you want to eat it?

346
00:18:08,440 --> 00:18:09,300
Yes, please.

347
00:18:09,380 --> 00:18:10,080
I'd love that.

348
00:18:16,380 --> 00:18:20,740
There's doors all over this place, but seems like only two of them lead outside, huh?

349
00:18:21,080 --> 00:18:22,560
No getting ambushed, at least.

350
00:18:22,560 --> 00:18:29,980
This house seems like it'll be comfortable to live in.

351
00:18:30,160 --> 00:18:32,140
Why do they have seven bathrooms, though?

352
00:18:32,740 --> 00:18:34,280
All right, let's sleep here, then.

353
00:18:34,440 --> 00:18:34,840
Yay!

354
00:18:35,460 --> 00:18:38,240
It's been ages since I've slept in a real bed.

355
00:18:38,280 --> 00:18:40,380
We still gotta use our sleeping bags, you know.

356
00:18:47,580 --> 00:18:49,740
I'm sorry to be intruding like this.

357
00:18:49,740 --> 00:18:52,860
Once we get enough rest, then we'll be on our way.

358
00:18:53,480 --> 00:18:54,420
Hey, what's up?

359
00:18:55,100 --> 00:18:55,780
A resident.

360
00:18:56,420 --> 00:18:57,520
She's letting us stay.

361
00:18:58,220 --> 00:18:59,240
Is that so?

362
00:18:59,740 --> 00:19:00,520
That's great.

363
00:19:02,080 --> 00:19:05,620
There are only four of them, so we'll have to share a sleeping bag.

364
00:19:05,880 --> 00:19:09,400
We haven't really slept in the same bed since our school days, have we?

365
00:19:09,460 --> 00:19:10,840
I wonder if we'll both fit.

366
00:19:11,720 --> 00:19:14,820
I feel like I've probably gotten a lot taller since then, huh?

367
00:19:14,980 --> 00:19:16,880
Oh, don't be so ridiculous!

368
00:19:16,880 --> 00:19:22,700
I don't care if you've grown, you're still a runt in my eyes.

369
00:19:26,840 --> 00:19:28,720
I'm glad that you're with us again.

370
00:19:30,360 --> 00:19:31,420
Yeah, me too.

371
00:19:34,740 --> 00:19:36,760
I'm gonna go say goodnight to my brother.

372
00:19:41,440 --> 00:19:41,840
Brother?

373
00:19:41,840 --> 00:19:44,200
What is it?

374
00:19:52,400 --> 00:19:53,640
This injury here.

375
00:19:54,240 --> 00:19:55,280
You were being reckless.

376
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:56,840
Why would you do...

377
00:19:57,540 --> 00:20:06,620
Maybe if a certain sister of mine hadn't been reckless first, I wouldn't have even had that injury.

378
00:20:06,980 --> 00:20:07,340
Huh?

379
00:20:07,340 --> 00:20:10,160
So don't ever do anything like that again.

380
00:20:10,640 --> 00:20:13,340
I honestly can't say I even recall what I...

381
00:20:15,340 --> 00:20:21,520
I won't do it again.

382
00:20:25,020 --> 00:20:26,960
Goodnight, big brother.

383
00:20:27,820 --> 00:20:28,680
You too.

384
00:20:29,220 --> 00:20:29,820
Sleep tight.

385
00:20:31,340 --> 00:20:32,260
Huh?

386
00:20:32,260 --> 00:20:33,400
You too.

387
00:20:33,400 --> 00:21:03,380
Thank you.

